## ✦ What it does

Study Planner is an AI-assisted learning application for learners who want to study from their own material rather than rely on a generic chatbot.

It combines:

- **Structured planning** — organize topics and subtopics, assign priorities, and generate a schedule around a date range and daily time budget.
- **Personal study material** — upload one or more PDFs and index their contents for later retrieval.
- **Active recall** — generate quizzes and flip-through flashcards for selected subtopics.
- **Grounded Q&A** — ask questions against retrieved chunks from the material you uploaded.
- **Persistent local data** — keep topics, schedules, indexed content, uploaded files, and model caches across Docker restarts.

> **Scope:** This is a local, single-user project. AI features use an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, configured by default for LM Studio running on the host machine.

## ✨ Features

| Area | Included |
| --- | --- |
| **Planning** | Prioritized topics, subtopics, date-bounded schedules, study/review/quiz sessions, completion tracking |
| **Material ingestion** | Multi-file and folder PDF uploads, text extraction, overlapping chunking, duplicate detection with SHA-256 |
| **Retrieval** | Persistent ChromaDB collection, semantic retrieval, cross-encoder reranking, topic-scoped search |
| **AI study tools** | Retrieval-grounded explanations, multiple-choice quizzes, generated flashcards, schedule generation |
| **Web experience** | Next.js dashboard with dedicated Topics, Upload, Chat, Quiz, Flashcards, and Schedule views |
| **Portability** | Separate frontend/backend Docker images and a Docker Compose workflow |

## 🧭 How it works

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    U([Learner]) --> FE[Next.js frontend]
    FE --> API[FastAPI REST API]

    API --> DB[(SQLite + SQLAlchemy)]
    API --> PDF[PDF ingestion]
    API --> GEN[AI generation]

    PDF --> TXT[Extract text]
    TXT --> CHUNK[Split into chunks]
    CHUNK --> EMBED[all-MiniLM-L6-v2]
    EMBED --> VDB[(Persistent ChromaDB)]

    GEN --> SEARCH[Retrieve up to 20 chunks]
    SEARCH --> RERANK[Cross-encoder reranking]
    RERANK --> CONTEXT[Top 3 context chunks]
    CONTEXT --> LLM[OpenAI-compatible LLM]
    LLM --> API
```

### Retrieval and generation pipeline

1. A PDF is saved and identified by a SHA-256 content hash.
2. Text is extracted with `pypdf` and split into overlapping chunks.
3. `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` creates an embedding for each chunk.
4. Chunks and metadata are persisted in the `Study_materials` ChromaDB collection.
5. A question or generation request retrieves up to 20 candidate chunks.
6. `cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2` reranks those candidates.
7. The top three chunks are sent as context to the configured LLM.

The same retrieval path supports study-material explanations, quiz generation, and flashcard generation. The LLM is instructed to use the supplied context rather than treat the request as unrestricted general chat.

